Now we need to allocate vehicle to shift_candidate_alpha (step7). We'll do that after creating shift_candidate_alpha.

Now we need to prepare shift_candidate_alpha:

- attach_task_profile shift_candidate_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
- confirm_candidate_preparedness shift_candidate_alpha route_task_profile_alpha

Now we need to load container onto leg etc.

But before loading container we need to assemble transport leg and authorize loading.

We need origin and destination availabilities locked and confirmed (we have after lock steps). Nodes are ready (after activation). So we can assemble transport leg.

Now we need to ensure we have not detached task profile from origin_availability_alpha after lock; we detached at step8 and step17. That's fine; lock does not require task profile linked.

Now assemble_transport_leg requires origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_node_linked, destination_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available.

All satisfied.

Now authorize_transport_leg_loading requires origin_availability_locked and candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile.

Thus we need to attach task profile to origin_availability_alpha again (since we detached). We'll need to attach again before authorize.

Now load_container_onto_leg requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_alpha (we will have), candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_alpha transport_leg_alpha (we have from init), candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_alpha loading_container_alpha (we have from init), loading_container_available loading_container_alpha (we have not used it yet; we have two containers alpha and beta; we haven't used any yet), transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not loading_container_loaded loading_container_alpha.

Thus we need to ensure loading_container_alpha is available. It is initially available; we haven't used it. Good.

Now after load_container_onto_leg we get loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked, and not loading_container_available.

Now stage_schedule_candidate requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_alpha, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_loaded, loading_container_leg_linked, candidate_task_profile_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not candidate_staged_for_loading.

We have origin_leg_loaded? Not set yet (assemble_transport_leg does not set origin_leg_loaded). So origin_leg_loaded false. Good.

Thus we can stage.

Now verify_loading_profile_nominal requires candidate_staged_for_loading, candidate_skill_certificate_linked, candidate_operator_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_loading_verified.

We have not destination_leg_loaded (still false). Good.

Thus we need skill_certificate and operator linked.

Now verify_compliance_certificate requires operator_alignment_confirmed and candidate_compliance_certificate_linked.

Thus we need to apply operational constraint and confirm operator alignment before verification.

Thus after loading and staging, we need to assign skill certificate and operator to shift_candidate_alpha, then apply operational constraint, confirm operator alignment, assign compliance certificate, verify compliance, finalize.

But note verify_loading_profile_nominal requires candidate_operator_linked (we will have after assign_operator_resource). Also requires candidate_skill_certificate_linked (after assign_skill_certificate). Good.

Now we need to ensure we have not used the operator elsewhere causing it to be unavailable. We released operator from origin and destination after lock. So operator is available again.

Thus we can assign operator to shift_candidate_alpha.

Now we need to ensure we have not used the skill certificate elsewhere; it's available.

Now we need to ensure we have not used the compliance certificate elsewhere; it's available.

Now we need to ensure we have not used the operational_constraint_alpha elsewhere; it's available and linked to shift_candidate_alpha.

Now we need to ensure we have not used the loading_container_alpha elsewhere; we will use it for loading container onto leg.

Now we need to ensure we have not used the transport_leg_alpha elsewhere; we will assemble and authorize.

Now we need to ensure we have not used the route_task_profile_alpha more than available at any time; we will attach/detach as needed.

Now we need to ensure we have not used the vehicle units incorrectly; we allocated each to a candidate and never deallocated.

Now we need to ensure we have not accidentally made any of the goal predicates false via side effects. For example, after we allocate vehicle_unit_alpha to origin_availability_alpha, we have vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha true. That's goal. Good.

Now we need to ensure we have not inadvertently dispatched any candidate (which would set dispatched true and maybe affect goal? Goal does not require not dispatched for any; but we might have dispatched something inadvertently; but we don't have any dispatch actions in plan, so fine.

Now we need to verify each step's preconditions.

